why check_pairs borrows a and b from Program.pair: Option<(String, String)> and visits the fixed [a, b] array. Both positions are ends, so the rewrite visits a then b and preserves early returns and duplicate/aliased references. The counter advances at most twice; peek moves only shared String references, with no user callback or destructor effect. The body and its outcome/diagnostics are unchanged. Compiled actual-candidate controls hold order and early returns, and refuse first/last-only and wider-array equivalence claims (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.8.2).
